  "response": "Here is a Python function `shortest_path(edges, start, end)` that computes the shortest path between two nodes in a directed weighted graph. It handles edge cases such as same start and end, negative weights (via `ValueError`), unreachable targets, and reconstructs the correct node sequence using Dijkstra's algorithm.\n\n```python\nimport heapq\n\ndef shortest_path(edges, start, end):\n    \"\"\"\n    Compute the shortest path between two nodes in a directed weighted graph.\n    \n    Args:\n        edges: List of (from_node, to_node, weight) tuples\n        start: Starting node\n        end: Target node\n    \n    Returns:\n        Tuple of (distance, path) where distance is shortest total weight and \n        path is ordered list of nodes. Returns (None, None) if no path exists.\n    \n    Raises:\n        ValueError: If any edge has negative weight.\n    \"\"\"\n    # Check for negative weights\n    for from_node, to_node, weight in edges:\n        if weight < 0:\n            raise ValueError(\"Negative edge weight is not allowed\")\n\n    # Handle same start and end\n    if start == end:\n        return (0, [start])\n\n    # Build graph using adjacency list with minimum edge weights\n    graph = {}\n    for from_node, to_node, weight in edges:\n        if from_node not in graph:\n            graph[from_node] = {}\n        current_weight = graph[from_node].get(to_node, float('inf'))\n        graph[from_node][to_node] = min(current_weight, weight)\n\n    # Check that start node has outgoing edges\n    if start not in graph or len(graph[start]) == 0:\n        return (None, None)\n\n    # Initialize distances and predecessor tracking\n    all_nodes = set()\n    for u in graph:\n        for v in graph[u]:\n            all_nodes.add(u)\n            all_nodes.add(v)\n\n    distances = {node: float('inf') for node in all_nodes}\n    previous = {}\n    distances[start] = 0\n    pq = [(0, start)]\n    visited = set()\n\n    # Dijkstra's algorithm\n    while pq:\n        current_dist, current_node = heapq.heappop(pq)\n\n        if current_node in visited or current_dist > distances[current_node]:\n            continue\n        visited.add(current_node)\n\n        for neighbor, weight in graph.get(current_node, {}).items():\n            new_dist = current_dist + weight\n            if new_dist < distances[neighbor]:\n                distances[neighbor] = new_dist\n                previous[neighbor] = current_node\n                heapq.heappush(pq, (new_dist, neighbor))\n\n    # Check if end is reachable\n    if distances[end] == float('inf'):\n        return (None, None)\n\n    # Reconstruct the path\n    path = []\n    node = end\n    while node != start:\n        if node not in previous:\n            return (None, None)  # Path cannot be reconstructed\n        path.append(node)\n        node = previous[node]\n    path.append(start)\n    path.reverse()\n\n    return (distances[end], path)\n```\n\n### Example Usage\n\n```python\n# Shortest path exists and is the optimal one\nedges = [(\"A\",\"B\",1), (\"B\",\"C\",2), (\"A\",\"C\",5)]\nprint(shortest_path(edges, \"A\", \"C\"))  # (3, ['A', 'B', 'C'])\n\n# Same start and end\nprint(shortest_path([(\"X\",\"Y\",3)], \"X\", \"X\"))  # (0, ['X'])\n\n# No path exists\nprint(shortest_path([(\"A\",\"B\",1)], \"A\", \"C\"))  # (None, None)\n\n# Negative weight should raise error\ntry:\n    edges = [(\"A\",\"B\",-1), (\"B\",\"C\",2)]\n    shortest_path(edges, \"A\", \"C\")\nexcept ValueError as e:\n    print(e)  # ValueError: Negative edge weight is not allowed\n```",
